CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pack expanded: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ nested in a compound type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.alias]/2, [temp.variadic]/5: holder_of<int &, long &> is
holder<char, int &, long &>: the i-th element of the expansion of
`typename id<A>::type...' substitutes the i-th element of the alias's
pack A.  template_mapt::apply substituted only a pattern that is the bare
pack; the A nested in id<A> stayed a name, later looked up where the
using function template's own pack A was visible, and became its first
element: holder<char, int &, int &>, and the conversion failed ("already
declared with different type", bin53).  The nested reference is now
substituted as well.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
